{%- comment %}
============ PROTOTYPE: FACT + FLAVOUR ============
Two lines instead of one. The fact line is built from short templates,
a few wordings per situation, and is the same at every sarcasm level. The flavour
line carries the personality: picked by the mood of the day, never
asked to carry a fact, absent at sarcasm 0.

Inserted by prototypes/fact-flavour/build.py ahead of THE PICTURE,
after the old hint is built, so both can be rendered side by side.
Reads only what the scenario logic above already worked out.
{%- endcomment %}
{%- assign fact_line = '' -%}
{%- assign flavour_line = '' -%}
{%- assign mood = '' -%}
{%- assign now_mood = '' -%}
{%- assign fl_now_pool = nil -%}
{%- assign fl_alone_all = nil -%}
{%- assign today_month = today_md | slice: 0, 2 -%}
{%- comment %}
Month tags ({M:..}) name the northern season. South of the equator the
seasons run six months on, so a December line about the cold shows there
in June. The latitude comes with the weather data.
{%- endcomment %}
{%- assign season_month = today_month -%}
{%- assign wx_lat = IDX_0.latitude | default: 0 | plus: 0 -%}
{%- if wx_lat < 0 -%}
  {%- assign sm = today_month | plus: 5 | modulo: 12 | plus: 1 -%}
  {%- if sm < 10 -%}{%- assign season_month = '0' | append: sm -%}{%- else -%}{%- assign season_month = sm | append: '' -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- assign flavour_topical = false -%}
{%- comment %}
The two switches (config/settings.next.yaml):
  Forecast            show_future_suggestions, the field that was there:
                      "Yes"/"No" saved before, true/false now. The words.
  What to Wear Next?  what_to_wear_next, true/false: the drawings.
Both can be on. The first beta had the drawings as a third Forecast value,
"visual": a fork with that saved keeps drawings without words.
The sarcastic line no longer needs either: it shows at On and 11 even on
the outfit alone.
{%- endcomment %}
{%- assign forecast_on = false -%}
{%- if show_future_suggestions == 'on' and sfs_check != 'visual' -%}{%- assign forecast_on = true -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- assign next_check = trmnl.plugin_settings.custom_fields_values.what_to_wear_next | append: '' | downcase | strip -%}
{%- assign next_on = false -%}
{%- if next_check == 'true' or next_check == 'on' or next_check == 'yes' or next_check == '1' or sfs_check == 'visual' -%}
  {%- assign next_on = true -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- comment %}
Which wording shows changes every hour, not once a day, so a day whose
weather doesn't change still reads differently in the afternoon. Each
pool takes (text_rot + its own offset) mod its size. Day and hour are
multiplied by primes larger than any pool (101, 103: coprime with every
size up to 100), so each step lands somewhere else in the pool instead
of on the next line, every line comes round, and someone who looks at
7:00 every morning sees the whole pool over the days, not a subset.
The screen changes when TRMNL next regenerates it: the weather's
current time moves every 15 minutes, so the merge variables change.
{%- endcomment %}
{%- assign text_rot = local_days | times: 101 -%}
{%- assign text_rot_h = local_hour | times: 103 -%}
{%- assign text_rot = text_rot | plus: text_rot_h -%}
{%- if is_error == false and texts_ok and texts.facts -%}
  {%- assign F = texts.facts -%}
  {%- if is_steady -%}
    {%- if local_hour >= 17 -%}
      {%- assign f_key = 'steady_evening' -%}
    {%- elsif band_rank >= 7 -%}
      {%- assign f_key = 'steady_hot' -%}
    {%- elsif band_rank <= 2 -%}
      {%- assign f_key = 'steady_cold' -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- assign f_key = 'steady' -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- assign f_key = temp_scenario -%}
    {%- if f_key == 'shorts_swing_back' and when_temp2 == '' -%}{%- assign f_key = 'shorts_swing' -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- comment %} Dangerous heat leads with water and shade, whatever else the day does. {%- endcomment %}
  {%- if heat_danger and F.heat_danger -%}{%- assign f_key = 'heat_danger' -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- comment %}
  The garment on screen, for the arc keys: {G} the garment, {GP} its
  pronoun, {GV} garment with its verb (German agrees "kann"/"können").
  {%- endcomment %}
  {%- assign f_g = '' -%}
  {%- assign f_gp = '' -%}
  {%- assign f_gv = '' -%}
  {%- if band_rank <= 4 -%}
    {%- assign fgi = band_rank | minus: 1 -%}
    {%- assign f_g = F.garments[fgi] -%}
    {%- assign f_gp = F.garments_pron[fgi] -%}
    {%- assign f_gv = F.garments_verb[fgi] -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- comment %}
  Each situation has several wordings, rotated by the hour like the
  flavour line (text_rot) but on their own offsets, so a run of the same
  weather doesn't show the same words.
  {%- endcomment %}
  {%- assign f_temp = '' -%}
  {%- assign f_list = F[f_key] -%}
  {%- if f_list -%}
    {%- assign f_n = f_list | size -%}
    {%- assign f_vi = text_rot | plus: 2 | modulo: f_n -%}
    {%- assign f_temp = f_list[f_vi] -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- assign f_temp = f_temp | replace: '{GV}', f_gv | replace: '{GP}', f_gp | replace: '{G}', f_g -%}
  {%- assign f_temp = f_temp | replace: '{WHEN2}', when_temp2 | replace: '{WHEN}', when_temp -%}
  {%- assign f_precip = '' -%}
  {%- if precip_scenario != '' -%}
    {%- assign pk = 'p_' | append: precip_scenario -%}
    {%- comment %} Snowing now: the snow wording, where the situation has one. {%- endcomment %}
    {%- if is_now_snow == 1 -%}
      {%- assign pks = pk | append: '_snow' -%}
      {%- if F[pks] -%}{%- assign pk = pks -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- comment %}
      Freezing rain in the window (WMO 56, 57, 66, 67): the ice warning.
      A thunderstorm (95, 96, 99): the storm wording. Each where the
      situation has one; freezing rain first.
      {%- endcomment %}
      {%- assign p_ice = false -%}
      {%- assign p_storm = false -%}
      {%- assign wx_codes = ',' | append: wmo | append: ',' -%}
      {%- if has_future_window and codes -%}
        {%- for i in (start_index..end_index) -%}
          {%- assign pi = probs[i] | default: 0 | plus: 0 -%}
          {%- if pi >= RAIN_LOW -%}{%- assign wx_codes = wx_codes | append: codes[i] | append: ',' -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if wx_codes contains ',56,' or wx_codes contains ',57,' or wx_codes contains ',66,' or wx_codes contains ',67,' -%}{%- assign p_ice = true -%}{%- endif -%}
      {%- if wx_codes contains ',95,' or wx_codes contains ',96,' or wx_codes contains ',99,' -%}{%- assign p_storm = true -%}{%- endif -%}
      {%- assign pki = pk | append: '_ice' -%}
      {%- assign pkt = pk | append: '_storm' -%}
      {%- if p_ice and F[pki] -%}
        {%- assign pk = pki -%}
      {%- elsif p_storm and F[pkt] -%}
        {%- assign pk = pkt -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- comment %}
    {WHENSTOP}: when the rain or snow falling now stops, from the first dry
    break. A wording that says it is skipped when there's no such time.
    {%- endcomment %}
    {%- assign when_stop = '' -%}
    {%- if stop_idx >= 0 and is_now_precip == 1 -%}
      {%- assign sgap = stop_idx | minus: now_index -%}
      {%- assign sh = local_hour | plus: sgap -%}
      {%- if sh > 23 -%}{%- assign sh = 23 -%}{%- endif -%}
      {%- assign sb = HOUR_BUCKET[sh] | plus: 0 -%}
      {%- if sb == now_bucket and sgap >= 1 and sgap <= 3 -%}
        {%- assign sgi = sgap | minus: 1 -%}
        {%- assign when_stop = RELATIVE[sgi] -%}
      {%- else -%}
        {%- assign when_stop = BUCKETS[sb] -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- assign p_list = F[pk] -%}
    {%- if p_list -%}
      {%- assign p_n = p_list | size -%}
      {%- assign p_vi = text_rot | plus: 3 | modulo: p_n -%}
      {%- for k in (1..p_n) -%}
        {%- assign p_cand = p_list[p_vi] -%}
        {%- unless p_cand contains '{WHENSTOP}' and when_stop == '' -%}
          {%- assign f_precip = p_cand | replace: '{WHENP}', when_precip | replace: '{WHENSTOP}', when_stop -%}
          {%- break -%}
        {%- endunless -%}
        {%- assign p_vi = p_vi | plus: 1 | modulo: p_n -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if is_steady and f_precip != '' -%}
    {%- assign fact_line = f_precip -%}
  {%- elsif f_precip != '' -%}
    {%- assign fact_line = f_temp | append: ' ' | append: f_precip -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- assign fact_line = f_temp -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- assign fact_line = fact_line | replace: '  ', ' ' | replace: ' .', '.' | replace: ' ,', ',' | strip -%}
  {%- assign marked = fact_line | replace: '. ', '.^^' | replace: '! ', '!^^' | replace: '? ', '?^^' -%}
  {%- assign sentences = marked | split: '^^' -%}
  {%- assign cased = '' -%}
  {%- for sentence in sentences -%}
    {%- assign s = sentence | strip -%}
    {%- assign head = s | slice: 0 | upcase -%}
    {%- assign tail = s | slice: 1, 400 -%}
    {%- if forloop.first -%}
      {%- assign cased = head | append: tail -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- assign cased = cased | append: ' ' | append: head | append: tail -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
  {%- assign fact_line = cased -%}

  {%- comment %} The mood of the day, for the flavour line. First match wins. {%- endcomment %}
  {%- assign temp_prefix = temp_scenario | slice: 0, 2 -%}
  {%- if precip_scenario == 'snow_coming' or is_now_snow == 1 -%}
    {%- assign mood = 'snow' -%}
  {%- elsif precip_scenario != '' -%}
    {%- assign mood = 'wet' -%}
  {%- elsif is_steady and local_hour >= 22 -%}
    {%- comment %} Only this late may a line mention bed: at 19:00 people check before going out. {%- endcomment %}
    {%- assign mood = 'night' -%}
  {%- elsif is_steady and local_hour >= 18 -%}
    {%- assign mood = 'evening' -%}
  {%- elsif is_arc and temp_scenario != 'arc_warmer' -%}
    {%- comment %}
    Only an arc that wants the layer back. When the evening stays warmer
    than the morning, the fact says "can come off and stay off", and
    "Erst zu warm, dann zu kalt" or "An, aus, wieder an" would contradict
    it: that day falls through to hot or warming.
    {%- endcomment %}
    {%- assign mood = 'fickle' -%}
  {%- elsif band_rank >= 7 or up_rank >= 7 -%}
    {%- assign mood = 'hot' -%}
  {%- elsif band_rank <= 2 -%}
    {%- assign mood = 'cold' -%}
  {%- elsif is_steady and band_rank >= 4 -%}
    {%- assign mood = 'nice' -%}
  {%- elsif temp_prefix == 'c_' -%}
    {%- comment %} An ordinary day, split by what it actually does: a layer is needed later... {%- endcomment %}
    {%- assign mood = 'cooling' -%}
  {%- elsif temp_scenario != '' -%}
    {%- comment %} ...something comes off later (the commonest of all)... {%- endcomment %}
    {%- assign mood = 'warming' -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- comment %} ...or a steady, cool jacket day. {%- endcomment %}
    {%- assign mood = 'cool' -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- comment %}
  What the Now drawing shows, for the "now" lines (now_10 / now_11): they
  stand alone and agree with the drawing, so they fit every screen, the
  outfit alone included. Rain and snow only while they fall: that's when
  the drawing has them.
  {%- endcomment %}
  {%- if is_now_snow == 1 -%}
    {%- assign now_mood = 'snow' -%}
  {%- elsif is_now_precip == 1 -%}
    {%- assign now_mood = 'wet' -%}
  {%- elsif local_hour >= 22 -%}
    {%- assign now_mood = 'night' -%}
  {%- elsif local_hour >= 18 -%}
    {%- assign now_mood = 'evening' -%}
  {%- elsif band_rank >= 7 -%}
    {%- assign now_mood = 'hot' -%}
  {%- elsif band_rank <= 2 -%}
    {%- assign now_mood = 'cold' -%}
  {%- elsif band_rank >= 4 -%}
    {%- assign now_mood = 'nice' -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- assign now_mood = 'cool' -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if sarcasm_level != '0' -%}
    {%- assign fl_key = 'flavour_' | append: sarcasm_level -%}
    {%- assign fl_lib = texts[fl_key] -%}
    {%- comment %}
    Two kinds of sarcastic line (owner, round 11). Under the forecast line,
    follow-ups (flavour_10 / _11, by the day's mood): they build on what it
    said ("Taking that layer off might be the highlight of your day").
    Everywhere else, standalone lines: the now lines (now_10 / _11, by what
    the Now drawing shows) and the day's own standalone lines (alone_10 /
    _11, by the day's mood: "Later it cools off. I saw that coming"). Two
    or three drawings add theirs in the panels block. No follow-ups for
    the mood: the standalone lines.
    {%- endcomment %}
    {%- assign now_key = 'now_' | append: sarcasm_level -%}
    {%- assign alone_key = 'alone_' | append: sarcasm_level -%}
    {%- assign fl_now_pool = texts[now_key][now_mood] -%}
    {%- assign fl_alone_pool = texts[alone_key][mood] -%}
    {%- assign fl_alone_all = fl_now_pool -%}
    {%- if fl_alone_pool and fl_now_pool -%}
      {%- assign fl_alone_all = fl_alone_pool | concat: fl_now_pool -%}
    {%- elsif fl_alone_pool -%}
      {%- assign fl_alone_all = fl_alone_pool -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- comment %}
    A texts file from before the now and day pools (13 October 2026): its
    lines are still by the day's mood. That happens when the texts URL is
    behind the markup (a fork's pinned commit, or jsDelivr still serving
    an old @main for a few hours after a release). Without this, two
    screens in three had no sarcastic line.
    {%- endcomment %}
    {%- if fl_alone_all == nil and texts[now_key] == nil -%}
      {%- comment %} Those files have no "cooling" lines: cooling days drew from "cool". {%- endcomment %}
      {%- if fl_lib[mood] -%}{%- assign fl_alone_all = fl_lib[mood] -%}{%- else -%}{%- assign fl_alone_all = fl_lib['cool'] -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- comment %}
    A follow-up goes by what the forecast line says, not by the mood: a
    cold day's line may say it stays cold or that the coat comes off. Ten
    groups, each one message: rain, snow (the umbrella or the snow; a
    rain sentence comes last when there are two), off (a layer comes off
    later), on (a layer is needed later), offon (off, then back on), hot
    (the line says water), steady, cold, evening, night. The heat easing
    a little (c_relief) says no water: the standalone lines.
    {%- endcomment %}
    {%- assign fu_key = '' -%}
    {%- if f_precip != '' -%}
      {%- if pk contains '_ice' -%}{%- assign fu_key = 'ice' -%}{%- elsif pk contains '_storm' -%}{%- assign fu_key = 'storm' -%}{%- elsif pk contains 'snow' -%}{%- assign fu_key = 'snow' -%}{%- else -%}{%- assign fu_key = 'rain' -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- case f_key -%}
        {%- when 'steady_evening' -%}
          {%- if local_hour >= 22 -%}{%- assign fu_key = 'night' -%}{%- else -%}{%- assign fu_key = 'evening' -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- when 'steady_hot', 'w_water' -%}{%- assign fu_key = 'hot' -%}
        {%- when 'steady_cold' -%}{%- assign fu_key = 'cold' -%}
        {%- when 'steady' -%}{%- assign fu_key = 'steady' -%}
        {%- when 'w_scarf', 'w_coat', 'w_jacket', 'w_hoodie', 'arc_warmer', 'shorts_early' -%}{%- assign fu_key = 'off' -%}
        {%- when 'c_scarf', 'c_coat', 'c_jacket', 'c_hoodie' -%}{%- assign fu_key = 'on' -%}
        {%- when 'arc_level', 'arc_colder' -%}{%- assign fu_key = 'offon' -%}
        {%- when 'shorts_swing', 'shorts_swing_back' -%}{%- assign fu_key = 'shorts' -%}
        {%- when 'pants_swing' -%}{%- assign fu_key = 'pants' -%}
        {%- when 'heat_danger' -%}{%- assign fu_key = 'scorch' -%}
      {%- endcase -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- comment %}
    The garment the forecast line names, for follow-ups that point back at
    it: {GP} its pronoun ("it"/"them", "sie"/"ihn"), {G} the garment. A
    line may also say which garments it fits: "{W:coat,jacket}…" (slugs
    scarf, coat, jacket, hoodie). Such lines are skipped on a forecast
    line that names no garment, or another one.
    {%- endcomment %}
    {%- assign fu_gi = -1 -%}
    {%- case f_key -%}
      {%- when 'w_scarf', 'c_scarf' -%}{%- assign fu_gi = 0 -%}
      {%- when 'w_coat', 'c_coat' -%}{%- assign fu_gi = 1 -%}
      {%- when 'w_jacket', 'c_jacket' -%}{%- assign fu_gi = 2 -%}
      {%- when 'w_hoodie', 'c_hoodie' -%}{%- assign fu_gi = 3 -%}
      {%- when 'arc_warmer', 'arc_level', 'arc_colder', 'shorts_swing', 'shorts_swing_back' -%}
        {%- if f_g != '' -%}{%- assign fu_gi = band_rank | minus: 1 -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- endcase -%}
    {%- assign fu_g = '' -%}
    {%- assign fu_gp = '' -%}
    {%- assign fu_gs = '' -%}
    {%- if fu_gi >= 0 -%}
      {%- assign fu_g = F.garments[fu_gi] -%}
      {%- assign fu_gp = F.garments_pron[fu_gi] -%}
      {%- assign fu_slugs = 'scarf,coat,jacket,hoodie' | split: ',' -%}
      {%- assign fu_gs = ',' | append: fu_slugs[fu_gi] | append: ',' -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- comment %} A new group with no lines yet borrows its neighbour's. {%- endcomment %}
    {%- unless fl_lib[fu_key] -%}
      {%- case fu_key -%}
        {%- when 'ice', 'storm' -%}{%- assign fu_key = 'rain' -%}
        {%- when 'shorts' -%}{%- assign fu_key = 'off' -%}
        {%- when 'pants' -%}{%- assign fu_key = 'on' -%}
        {%- when 'scorch' -%}{%- assign fu_key = 'hot' -%}
      {%- endcase -%}
    {%- endunless -%}
    {%- assign fl_pool = fl_alone_all -%}
    {%- if forecast_on and fact_line != '' and fu_key != '' and fl_lib[fu_key] -%}
      {%- assign fl_pool = fl_lib[fu_key] -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- comment %} A seasonal day with nothing else to say gets its own lines. {%- endcomment %}
    {%- assign fl_theme = false -%}
    {%- if is_steady and active_theme != '' -%}
      {%- assign th_key = 'theme_' | append: active_theme -%}
      {%- if fl_lib[th_key] -%}
        {%- assign fl_pool = fl_lib[th_key] -%}
        {%- assign fl_theme = true -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- comment %}
    Special days (round 16), on a day with nothing else to say and every
    other hour, so the weather keeps its say: the clock change (that Sunday
    and the Monday after; Europe, the US and Canada, by the forecast's time
    zone), the longest and shortest day (swapped south of the equator),
    Monday mornings and Friday afternoons. A seasonal theme day wins.
    {%- endcomment %}
    {%- if is_steady and fl_theme == false -%}
      {%- assign day_key = '' -%}
      {%- assign dmon = today_md | slice: 0, 2 -%}
      {%- assign dday = today_md | slice: 3, 2 | plus: 0 -%}
      {%- assign tz_probe = ',' | append: IDX_0.timezone | append: ',' -%}
      {%- assign dst_rule = '' -%}
      {%- if tz_probe contains ',Europe/' -%}{%- assign dst_rule = 'eu' -%}{%- endif -%}
      {%- if ',Europe/Moscow,Europe/Minsk,Europe/Istanbul,Europe/Kaliningrad,Europe/Samara,Europe/Volgograd,Europe/Saratov,Europe/Ulyanovsk,Europe/Astrakhan,Europe/Kirov,' contains tz_probe -%}{%- assign dst_rule = '' -%}{%- endif -%}
      {%- if ',America/New_York,America/Chicago,America/Denver,America/Los_Angeles,America/Anchorage,America/Juneau,America/Boise,America/Detroit,America/Indiana/Indianapolis,America/Kentucky/Louisville,America/Toronto,America/Montreal,America/Vancouver,America/Edmonton,America/Winnipeg,America/Halifax,America/St_Johns,America/Moncton,' contains tz_probe -%}{%- assign dst_rule = 'na' -%}{%- endif -%}
      {%- if dst_rule == 'eu' -%}
        {%- if dmon == '03' and dday >= 25 and weekday_idx == 0 -%}{%- assign day_key = 'dst_spring' -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- if dmon == '03' and dday >= 26 and weekday_idx == 1 -%}{%- assign day_key = 'dst_spring' -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- if today_md == '04-01' and weekday_idx == 1 -%}{%- assign day_key = 'dst_spring' -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- if dmon == '10' and dday >= 25 and weekday_idx == 0 -%}{%- assign day_key = 'dst_fall' -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- if dmon == '10' and dday >= 26 and weekday_idx == 1 -%}{%- assign day_key = 'dst_fall' -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- if today_md == '11-01' and weekday_idx == 1 -%}{%- assign day_key = 'dst_fall' -%}{%- endif -%}
      {%- elsif dst_rule == 'na' -%}
        {%- if dmon == '03' and weekday_idx == 0 -%}
          {%- if dday >= 8 and dday <= 14 -%}{%- assign day_key = 'dst_spring' -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- elsif dmon == '03' and weekday_idx == 1 -%}
          {%- if dday >= 9 and dday <= 15 -%}{%- assign day_key = 'dst_spring' -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- elsif dmon == '11' and weekday_idx == 0 -%}
          {%- if dday <= 7 -%}{%- assign day_key = 'dst_fall' -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- elsif dmon == '11' and weekday_idx == 1 -%}
          {%- if dday >= 2 and dday <= 8 -%}{%- assign day_key = 'dst_fall' -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if day_key == '' -%}
        {%- if today_md == '06-21' -%}
          {%- if wx_lat < 0 -%}{%- assign day_key = 'shortest' -%}{%- else -%}{%- assign day_key = 'longest' -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- elsif today_md == '12-21' -%}
          {%- if wx_lat < 0 -%}{%- assign day_key = 'longest' -%}{%- else -%}{%- assign day_key = 'shortest' -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- elsif weekday_idx == 1 and local_hour < 12 -%}
          {%- assign day_key = 'monday' -%}
        {%- elsif weekday_idx == 5 and local_hour >= 12 -%}
          {%- assign day_key = 'friday' -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- assign dk = 'day_' | append: day_key -%}
      {%- assign dhalf = local_hour | modulo: 2 -%}
      {%- comment %} Mondays and Fridays come every week: not until there are three lines to rotate. {%- endcomment %}
      {%- assign dmin = 1 -%}
      {%- if day_key == 'monday' or day_key == 'friday' -%}{%- assign dmin = 3 -%}{%- endif -%}
      {%- assign dn = fl_lib[dk] | size -%}
      {%- if day_key != '' and dhalf == 0 and dn >= dmin -%}
        {%- assign fl_pool = fl_lib[dk] -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if fl_pool -%}
      {%- assign fl_n = fl_pool | size -%}
      {%- assign fl_i = text_rot | plus: 5 | modulo: fl_n -%}
      {%- comment %}
      A line may carry the months it shows in, as a tag build_pools.py puts
      in front: "{M:10,11}Every year everyone's surprised…". In another
      month the next line of the pool shows instead.
      {%- endcomment %}
      {%- assign fl_month = ',' | append: season_month | append: ',' -%}
      {%- for k in (1..fl_n) -%}
        {%- assign fl_cand = fl_pool[fl_i] -%}
        {%- assign fl_ok = true -%}
        {%- if fl_cand contains '{M:' -%}
          {%- assign fl_tag = fl_cand | split: '{M:' | last | split: '}' | first -%}
          {%- assign fl_tags = ',' | append: fl_tag | append: ',' -%}
          {%- unless fl_tags contains fl_month -%}{%- assign fl_ok = false -%}{%- endunless -%}
          {%- assign fl_prefix = '{M:' | append: fl_tag | append: '}' -%}
          {%- assign fl_cand = fl_cand | remove_first: fl_prefix -%}
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if fl_cand contains '{W:' -%}
          {%- assign fl_tag = fl_cand | split: '{W:' | last | split: '}' | first -%}
          {%- assign fl_tags = ',' | append: fl_tag | append: ',' -%}
          {%- if fu_gs == '' -%}
            {%- assign fl_ok = false -%}
          {%- else -%}
            {%- unless fl_tags contains fu_gs -%}{%- assign fl_ok = false -%}{%- endunless -%}
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- assign fl_prefix = '{W:' | append: fl_tag | append: '}' -%}
          {%- assign fl_cand = fl_cand | remove_first: fl_prefix -%}
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if fl_cand contains '{G' and fu_g == '' -%}{%- assign fl_ok = false -%}{%- endif -%}
        {%- if fl_ok -%}
          {%- assign flavour_line = fl_cand | replace: '{GP}', fu_gp | replace: '{G}', fu_g -%}
          {%- break -%}
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- assign fl_i = fl_i | plus: 1 | modulo: fl_n -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment %}
    ============ TOPICAL LINES ============
    Lines about current events, written with the owner and voted like the
    rest (.claude/skills/topical). Each carries a window and shows only
    inside it, so an expired line needs no republish; tools/topical.py
    prunes it from the file later.

      {"text": "...", "from": "2026-10-25", "until": "2026-10-29",
       "region": "UK,IE", "moods": "cold,wet"}

    region and moods are optional. A line shows on the first day of its
    window and then about one day in three, rotating with whatever else
    is active; the other days keep the mood's line, so a week of one joke
    doesn't wear thin. A seasonal theme day keeps its own lines. Off
    unless the topical_lines field is "on": installs from before the field
    have no value, so they never see news they didn't ask for.
    {%- endcomment %}
    {%- assign topical_raw = trmnl.plugin_settings.custom_fields_values.topical_lines | default: 'off' | downcase | strip -%}
    {%- assign tp_key = 'topical_' | append: sarcasm_level -%}
    {%- assign tp_list = texts[tp_key] -%}
    {%- if topical_raw == 'on' and fl_theme == false and tp_list -%}
      {%- comment %}
      Region from the forecast's own time zone (Open-Meteo, timezone=auto),
      which follows the device's location, not the account's.
      {%- endcomment %}
      {%- if IDX_0 -%}{%- assign tp_tz = IDX_0.timezone | default: '' -%}{%- else -%}{%- assign tp_tz = timezone | default: '' -%}{%- endif -%}
      {%- assign tp_probe = ',' | append: tp_tz | append: ',' -%}
      {%- assign tp_region = '' -%}
      {%- assign US_ZONES = ',America/New_York,America/Chicago,America/Denver,America/Los_Angeles,America/Phoenix,America/Anchorage,America/Detroit,America/Boise,America/Juneau,America/Sitka,America/Nome,America/Yakutat,America/Metlakatla,America/Adak,America/Menominee,Pacific/Honolulu,' -%}
      {%- if tp_probe == ',Europe/Berlin,' or tp_probe == ',Europe/Busingen,' -%}
        {%- assign tp_region = 'DE' -%}
      {%- elsif tp_probe == ',Europe/Vienna,' -%}
        {%- assign tp_region = 'AT' -%}
      {%- elsif tp_probe == ',Europe/Zurich,' -%}
        {%- assign tp_region = 'CH' -%}
      {%- elsif tp_probe == ',Europe/London,' -%}
        {%- assign tp_region = 'UK' -%}
      {%- elsif tp_probe == ',Europe/Dublin,' -%}
        {%- assign tp_region = 'IE' -%}
      {%- elsif US_ZONES contains tp_probe or tp_tz contains 'America/Indiana/' or tp_tz contains 'America/Kentucky/' or tp_tz contains 'America/North_Dakota/' -%}
        {%- assign tp_region = 'US' -%}
      {%- elsif tp_tz contains 'Australia/' -%}
        {%- assign tp_region = 'AU' -%}
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- assign tp_region_probe = ',' | append: tp_region | append: ',' -%}
      {%- assign tp_mood_probe = ',' | append: mood | append: ',' -%}
      {%- assign tp_today = today_year | append: '-' | append: today_md -%}
      {%- assign tp_cycle = local_days | modulo: 3 -%}
      {%- assign tp_joined = '' -%}
      {%- assign tp_n = 0 -%}
      {%- for t in tp_list -%}
        {%- if t.from <= tp_today and t.until >= tp_today -%}
          {%- assign tp_ok = true -%}
          {%- if t.region and t.region != '' -%}
            {%- assign tp_regions = ',' | append: t.region | remove: ' ' | append: ',' -%}
            {%- unless tp_region != '' and tp_regions contains tp_region_probe -%}{%- assign tp_ok = false -%}{%- endunless -%}
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if t.moods and t.moods != '' -%}
            {%- assign tp_moods = ',' | append: t.moods | remove: ' ' | append: ',' -%}
            {%- unless tp_moods contains tp_mood_probe -%}{%- assign tp_ok = false -%}{%- endunless -%}
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if tp_ok and t.from == tp_today or tp_ok and tp_cycle == 0 -%}
            {%- if tp_n == 0 -%}
              {%- assign tp_joined = t.text -%}
            {%- else -%}
              {%- assign tp_joined = tp_joined | append: '~|~' | append: t.text -%}
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- assign tp_n = tp_n | plus: 1 -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
      {%- if tp_n > 0 -%}
        {%- assign tp_texts = tp_joined | split: '~|~' -%}
        {%- assign tp_i = local_days | divided_by: 3 | modulo: tp_n -%}
        {%- assign flavour_line = tp_texts[tp_i] -%}
        {%- assign flavour_topical = true -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
